#
# THERE IS NO PRODUCTION DOCKER BUILD IN THIS REPOSITORY, and this file is here to keep it that
# way cheaply.
#
# Images are built by Bazel — see //services/go_vanity:image for the reference target — because
# tools/analysis/check_build_toolchain_contract.py forbids production Dockerfiles. Bazel never
# sends a build context to a daemon, so nothing in the release path reads this file.
#
# What does read it is an ad-hoc `docker build .` typed by a person. Without this file that
# command uploads the entire working tree as context: the .git directory, .venv, node_modules,
# every model fixture, and any .env sitting in a service directory. Denying everything makes
# that command fail immediately and obviously instead of quietly shipping a credential into a
# layer.
#
# If you are adding a Dockerfile: don't, unless it is genuinely dev-only, in which case it needs
# the MINDCLADE_DEV_ONLY=1 marker the contract check looks for. Production images are Bazel
# oci_image targets. //services/go_vanity is the worked example — go_library, a cross-compiled
# go_binary, pkg_tar, oci_image, oci_push.

*
